WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.662
Do not assume every view is writable.

00:00:02.662 --> 00:00:06.862
A simple one-table view may support automatic updates.

00:00:06.862 --> 00:00:11.962
A join or aggregate view does not have the same direct row mapping.

00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:18.387
Materialized views are stored query results, not ordinary write-through interfaces.

00:00:18.387 --> 00:00:24.202
Always check the actual PostgreSQL behavior for the view definition you are designing.

00:00:24.202 --> 00:00:31.377
Connect this idea to an analytics team exposing a stable reporting view to dashboard users.

00:00:31.377 --> 00:00:37.457
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.457 --> 00:00:45.262
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.262 --> 00:00:51.672
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.672 --> 00:00:57.989
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
